sbook><name>NIPPON STEEL CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKASHITA MASAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AKASHI, TOORU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAMAUZU, SHUUICHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KONDOU, YASUMITSU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NIPPON STEEL CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKASHITA, MASAO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>AKASHI TOORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HAMAUZU SHUUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KONDOU YASUMITSU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKASHITA MASAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AKASHI, TOORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAMAUZU, SHUUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KONDOU, YASUMITSU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKASHITA, MASAO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method of efficiently suppressing and removing scale in a hot rolling process of a steel product so as to remarkably shorten a pickling processing time in the next process, comprising the steps of applying a DC or AC of 0.1 to 10&lt;5&gt; A/m&lt;2&gt; per unit surface area from pinch rolls (2) and a roll (6) or an apron guide (7) on the outside of a hot rolling mill (1) to a metal material (11) in a water cooling process for the metal material (11) at 100 to 1200  DEG C and/or spraying the cooling water with a pH value of -2 to 4 from a cooling header (4) and the apron guide (7) to the metal material (11) so as to remove scales.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé permettant d'éliminer et d'enlever efficacement des écailles dans un processus de laminage à chaud d'un produit en acier, ce procédé permettant de raccourcir considérablement le temps de traitement par décapage au cours de l'étape suivante. Le procédé de cette invention consiste tout d'abord à appliquer sur un corps métallique (11) un courant continu ou alternatif variant entre 0,1 et 10&lt;5&gt; A/m&lt;2&gt; par aire spécifique unitaire, au moyen de rouleaux pinceurs (2) et d'un rouleau (6), ou d'un guide (7) pour le tablier du chariot, placé du coté extérieur d'une installation de laminage à chaud (1). Ce procédé consiste ensuite à soumettre ledit corps métallique (11) à un processus de refroidissement par eau entre 100 et 1200  DEG C, et/ou à pulvériser l'eau de refroidissement, qui présente une valeur pH située entre  2 et 4, depuis une tête de pulvérisation (4) et le guide (7) pour le tablier du chariot jusque sur le corps métallique (11), et ce afin d'enlever les écailles de ce corps.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>